{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"One concrete mismatch is in `foreach` by reference: Zend separates at `FE_RESET_RW`, but `FE_FETCH_RW` then accesses iterator buckets directly. Routing every element through the revision’s separating write fetch changes copy-during-loop behavior. I also confirmed that unset needs a non-vivifying fetch mode, and that object destruction needs a post-destructor refcount check for resurrection."}}
